    <briefdescription>
<para>Default propagation of shadow and/or origin. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class implements the general case of shadow propagation, used in all cases where we don&apos;t know and/or don&apos;t care about what the operation actually does. It converts all input shadow values to a common type (extending or truncating as necessary), and bitwise OR&apos;s them.</para>
<para>This is much cheaper than inserting checks (i.e. requiring inputs to be fully initialized), and less prone to false positives.</para>
<para>This class also implements the general case of origin propagation. For a Nary operation, result origin is set to the origin of an argument that is not entirely initialized. If there is more than one such arguments, the rightmost of them is picked. It does not matter which one is picked if all arguments are initialized. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
